WEBVTT

00:03.840 --> 00:05.560
So what is the cast function?

00:05.560 --> 00:09.200
It's going to go and convert a value to a different data type.

00:09.200 --> 00:11.840
So it turns one data type to another.

00:11.880 --> 00:12.200
All right.

00:12.200 --> 00:14.880
So now let's check the syntax of the cast I really like this one.

00:14.880 --> 00:18.520
It is not typical like format or syntax in SQL.

00:18.520 --> 00:21.280
So it says the cast is the function.

00:21.280 --> 00:23.480
And then inside it we need two things.

00:23.480 --> 00:27.560
But it's not separated like with the comma as we learned before with all other functions.

00:27.560 --> 00:30.000
But this time it's separated with the keyword s.

00:30.040 --> 00:35.160
So it's like the natural English you are saying cast the value as a data type.

00:35.160 --> 00:38.240
So you are casting the value to a new data type.

00:38.240 --> 00:44.280
So let's have this very simple example we have here cast the value 123 as integer.

00:44.280 --> 00:47.640
So previously it is string and it's going to be converted to integer.

00:47.640 --> 00:48.960
So as you can see it's very simple.

00:48.960 --> 00:53.720
Now in this example we are saying cast this value this string value as a date.

00:53.720 --> 00:55.800
So convert it from string to dates.

00:55.800 --> 01:00.960
So as you can see with the cast, we don't have here any option of formatting or styling the values.

01:00.960 --> 01:05.850
So it's only dedicated for casting the value from one data type to another one.

01:05.850 --> 01:07.570
So this is the syntax of the cast.

01:07.570 --> 01:10.250
It is very straightforward and really nice function.

01:10.290 --> 01:10.490
Okay.

01:10.530 --> 01:13.010
So now let's have a few examples about the cast.

01:13.010 --> 01:16.650
So let's go and convert a value from a string to integer.

01:16.650 --> 01:17.370
So it's very simple.

01:17.370 --> 01:18.890
We're going to say cast.

01:18.890 --> 01:20.090
So now we need the value.

01:20.090 --> 01:22.050
So let's go with the 123.

01:22.050 --> 01:23.290
So we have here a string.

01:23.290 --> 01:24.930
And then we're going to say as.

01:24.970 --> 01:26.930
And then we have to define the data type.

01:27.090 --> 01:28.970
So the data type going to be integer.

01:28.970 --> 01:29.770
So that's it.

01:29.770 --> 01:33.650
Let's give it the name like this string to integer.

01:33.810 --> 01:35.090
Let's go and execute it.

01:35.130 --> 01:36.570
Now you can see we got the value.

01:36.570 --> 01:39.450
But with the data type integer from string to integer.

01:39.490 --> 01:40.930
Now let's do the way round.

01:40.930 --> 01:42.690
We cast from integer to string.

01:42.690 --> 01:47.610
So we're going to say cast 123 as var char.

01:47.730 --> 01:52.010
And we're going to give it a name int to string.

01:52.210 --> 01:54.050
So let's go and execute it.

01:54.050 --> 01:56.210
Now in the output we have 123.

01:56.210 --> 01:59.090
But this time it has the data type varchar.

01:59.130 --> 02:00.850
Now let's go and work with the data.

02:00.850 --> 02:03.580
So we're going to go and convert a value.

02:03.980 --> 02:06.020
String value to date.

02:06.020 --> 02:09.380
So our value is going to be the usual one.

02:09.380 --> 02:11.420
And we want it from string to date.

02:11.420 --> 02:13.700
So we're going to have the data type as date.

02:14.020 --> 02:17.980
So let's give it a name string to date.

02:18.020 --> 02:19.660
Let's go and execute it.

02:19.700 --> 02:22.460
Now we're going to have this value with the data type date.

02:22.460 --> 02:23.460
So that's it.

02:23.500 --> 02:27.340
Now let's say that I would like to have this value but as date time.

02:27.580 --> 02:34.060
So I will just copy the whole thing and go to a new line and say date time to.

02:34.180 --> 02:37.380
So the name of this is going to be string to date time.

02:37.380 --> 02:39.460
Let's go and execute it now in the output.

02:39.460 --> 02:43.940
As you can see, we are getting not only the date but as well we are getting the time information.

02:43.940 --> 02:49.420
But now since we didn't provide SQL with any time information, it's going to go and show it as zeros.

02:49.460 --> 02:53.780
Now let's do one more casting where we change the data type from date time to date.

02:53.780 --> 02:55.740
So now we need our creation time.

02:56.900 --> 02:58.460
But we have to get it from the tables.

02:58.460 --> 03:02.500
So from sales orders let's go and execute it.

03:02.500 --> 03:05.070
So now in the output you can see the creation time is at a date time.

03:05.070 --> 03:08.510
We have the time information, but we are not interested about that time information.

03:08.510 --> 03:10.630
I would like to have this field as a date.

03:10.630 --> 03:11.590
So it's very simple.

03:11.590 --> 03:13.670
What we're going to do, we're going to say cast.

03:14.350 --> 03:20.270
Now the value is creation time and then the keyword as and we need it as a date.

03:20.270 --> 03:24.230
So we're going to give it a name date time to date.

03:24.430 --> 03:26.070
So let's go and execute it.

03:26.070 --> 03:30.790
Now as you can see in the output we got the creation time but only with the date information.

03:30.790 --> 03:35.670
We don't have anything about the time, so we get it as a date instead of date time.

03:35.670 --> 03:36.350
So that's it.

03:36.350 --> 03:38.790
This is amazing function in SQL and it's very simple.

03:38.790 --> 03:40.750
And we can use it only for casting.

03:40.750 --> 03:43.990
So only to change the data type from one to another.

03:43.990 --> 03:47.390
And we cannot use this function in order to change the format.

03:47.390 --> 03:51.430
So if you are casting you will get always the standard format from SQL.

03:55.510 --> 03:57.990
So now let's go and compare our functions side by side.

03:57.990 --> 04:01.230
So we have our three functions cast, convert and format.

04:01.230 --> 04:04.950
And we can do two things either casting or formatting.

04:04.950 --> 04:10.160
So by the casting for the first function cast, we can change any type to any other type, so there

04:10.160 --> 04:11.320
is no restriction at all.

04:11.360 --> 04:13.720
The same thing for the converts, the same thing.

04:13.720 --> 04:15.560
We can convert anything to anything.

04:15.560 --> 04:18.800
But for the format we can change only to string.

04:18.800 --> 04:24.960
So any data type like date or number to string value, because the main thing for the format is not

04:24.960 --> 04:26.080
changing the data type.

04:26.120 --> 04:30.920
Now, if you are talking about changing the format of the values, you cannot use the cast function

04:30.920 --> 04:32.520
in order to change the format.

04:32.520 --> 04:34.480
So the cast function is only for casting.

04:34.480 --> 04:35.200
It makes sense.

04:35.200 --> 04:36.280
Now about the convert.

04:36.280 --> 04:41.720
We can use it in order to change the format of the date and time, but we cannot use it in order to

04:41.720 --> 04:43.360
change the number formats.

04:43.400 --> 04:48.320
And for that we have a dedicated function called formats, so we can use it to change the format of

04:48.320 --> 04:50.840
the date and time and as well the numbers.

04:50.840 --> 04:53.480
So those are the main differences between those three functions.

04:53.520 --> 04:53.880
All right.

04:53.880 --> 04:59.440
So with those three functions we have learned how to do formatting and casting on date informations.

04:59.480 --> 05:02.640
